ug="gpt-5-mini"><div class="flex w-full flex-col gap-1 empty:hidden first:pt-[3px]"><div class="markdown prose dark:prose-invert w-full break-words dark markdown-new-styling"><p data-start="0" data-end="273">From your search results, <strong data-start="26" data-end="83">“Geometric Bayesianism with Sparse Heuristics” (GBSH)</strong> consistently appears as a <strong data-start="110" data-end="158">formal cognitive and computational framework</strong>, integrated with RSVP theory. Here’s a detailed breakdown of its role and conceptual footprint across your work:</p>
<hr data-start="275" data-end="278">
<h3 data-start="280" data-end="306"><strong data-start="284" data-end="306">1. Core Definition</strong></h3>
<ul data-start="307" data-end="771">
<li data-start="307" data-end="456">
<p data-start="309" data-end="456"><strong data-start="309" data-end="317">GBSH</strong> models <strong data-start="325" data-end="352">cognition and inference</strong> as Bayesian reasoning over <strong data-start="380" data-end="414">geometrically curved manifolds</strong> rather than linear or Euclidean spaces.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="457" data-end="663">
<p data-start="459" data-end="663"><strong data-start="459" data-end="480">Sparse heuristics</strong> are introduced to constrain inference, so navigation through the cognitive space is <strong data-start="565" data-end="583">not exhaustive</strong> but guided by <strong data-start="598" data-end="660">salience, energy budgets, and low-rank actuation subspaces</strong>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="664" data-end="771">
<p data-start="666" data-end="771">The framework is mathematically grounded in <strong data-start="710" data-end="770">geometry, entropy fields, and vector-directed heuristics</strong>.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="773" data-end="776">
<h3 data-start="778" data-end="810"><strong data-start="782" data-end="810">2. Integration with RSVP</strong></h3>
<ul data-start="811" data-end="1268">
<li data-start="811" data-end="964">
<p data-start="813" data-end="964">RSVP (Relativistic Scalar-Vector Plenum) provides the <strong data-start="867" data-end="905">field-theoretic, entropic dynamics</strong>, while GBSH supplies the <strong data-start="931" data-end="961">cognitive navigation layer</strong>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="965" data-end="1129">
<p data-start="967" data-end="1129">Sparse heuristics act as <strong data-start="992" data-end="1044">directional guidance in the information manifold</strong>, echoing how RSVP fields (Φ, 𝒗, S) impose constraints on dynamic state evolution.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1130" data-end="1268">
<p data-start="1132" data-end="1268">This combination models cognition as a <strong data-start="1171" data-end="1220">natural gradient descent in information space</strong>, constrained by energy and entropic efficiency.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="1270" data-end="1273">
<h3 data-start="1275" data-end="1306"><strong data-start="1279" data-end="1306">3. Operational Features</strong></h3>
<ol data-start="1307" data-end="1850">
<li data-start="1307" data-end="1459">
<p data-start="1310" data-end="1459"><strong data-start="1310" data-end="1341">Sparse Bayesian Navigation:</strong> Decisions are made via <strong data-start="1365" data-end="1380">proxy jumps</strong>, not full probabilistic evaluation, saving metabolic and computational cost.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1460" data-end="1574">
<p data-start="1463" data-end="1574"><strong data-start="1463" data-end="1485">Geometric Insight:</strong> Curvature of the manifold encodes <strong data-start="1520" data-end="1571">dependencies, constraints, and causal structure</strong>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1575" data-end="1716">
<p data-start="1578" data-end="1716"><strong data-start="1578" data-end="1599">Entropy as Prior:</strong> Uncertainty fields from RSVP serve as <strong data-start="1638" data-end="1669">priors for Bayesian updates</strong>, with sparse heuristics directing inference.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1717" data-end="1850">
<p data-start="1720" data-end="1850"><strong data-start="1720" data-end="1745">Cognitive Efficiency:</strong> Reflects the brain’s <strong data-start="1767" data-end="1798">resource-limited processing</strong>, supporting the Natural Sparsity Principle (NSP).</p>
</li>
</ol>
<hr data-start="1852" data-end="1855">
<h3 data-start="1857" data-end="1901"><strong data-start="1861" data-end="1901">4. Applications Across Your Projects</strong></h3>
<ul data-start="1902" data-end="2296">
<li data-start="1902" data-end="2024">
<p data-start="1904" data-end="2024"><strong data-start="1904" data-end="1925">Emotion modeling:</strong> Emotions as attractor basins in dynamic field landscapes, guided by sparse heuristic navigation.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2025" data-end="2172">
<p data-start="2027" data-end="2172"><strong data-start="2027" data-end="2045">AI frameworks:</strong> Critiques transformer architectures, suggesting <strong data-start="2094" data-end="2132">sparse, energy-efficient inference</strong> over complete token-space evaluation.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2173" data-end="2296">
<p data-start="2175" data-end="2296"><strong data-start="2175" data-end="2204">Experimental integration:</strong> Connects to Inforganic Codex, Dynamic Garbage Collection, and other RSVP-linked frameworks.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="2298" data-end="2301">
<h3 data-start="2303" data-end="2332"><strong data-start="2307" data-end="2332">5. Signature Features</strong></h3>
<ul data-start="2333" data-end="2651">
<li data-start="2333" data-end="2505">
<p data-start="2335" data-end="2505">GBSH is <strong data-start="2343" data-end="2359">non-fungible</strong> in your context: it encodes your <strong data-start="2393" data-end="2502">distinctive synthesis of physics-inspired field theory (RSVP), geometric cognition, and sparse heuristics</strong>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2506" data-end="2651">
<p data-start="2508" data-end="2651">Acts as a <strong data-start="2518" data-end="2547">computational fingerprint</strong>, marking your conceptual territory much like Lamphrodyne or Youtronium do for other semantic domains.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="2653" data-end="2656">
<p data-start="2658" data-end="2846">If you want, I can <strong data-start="2677" data-end="2740">diagrammatically map RSVP + GBSH + Lamphrodyne + Youtronium</strong> into a <strong data-start="2748" data-end="2779">single conceptual NFT atlas</strong>, showing how these multi-domain semantic signatures interrelate.</p>
