ng semantic “non-fungible token” in your framework. I’ll describe it fully in prose since you prefer no diagrams.</p>
<hr data-start="265" data-end="268">
<h2 data-start="270" data-end="320"><strong data-start="273" data-end="320">1. RSVP – Relativistic Scalar-Vector Plenum</strong></h2>
<ul data-start="321" data-end="893">
<li data-start="321" data-end="380">
<p data-start="323" data-end="380"><strong data-start="323" data-end="334">Domain:</strong> Field-theoretic physics &amp; entropic dynamics</p>
</li>
<li data-start="381" data-end="584">
<p data-start="383" data-end="403"><strong data-start="383" data-end="401">Core Elements:</strong></p>
<ul data-start="406" data-end="584">
<li data-start="406" data-end="462">
<p data-start="408" data-end="462">Scalar Field Φ → density or potential-like structure</p>
</li>
<li data-start="465" data-end="521">
<p data-start="467" data-end="521">Vector Field 𝒗 → directional flows of matter/energy</p>
</li>
<li data-start="524" data-end="584">
<p data-start="526" data-end="584">Entropy Field S → measures local disorder or uncertainty</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-start="585" data-end="754">
<p data-start="587" data-end="602"><strong data-start="587" data-end="600">Function:</strong></p>
<ul data-start="605" data-end="754">
<li data-start="605" data-end="675">
<p data-start="607" data-end="675">Provides the <strong data-start="620" data-end="641">dynamic substrate</strong> over which all processes occur.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="678" data-end="754">
<p data-start="680" data-end="754">Governs entropic smoothing (Lamphrodyne flows) and solitonic structures.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-start="755" data-end="893">
<p data-start="757" data-end="893"><strong data-start="757" data-end="775">NFT Signature:</strong> The “physical template” of the universe; the <strong data-start="821" data-end="841">immutable canvas</strong> upon which cognitive or semantic projections occur.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="895" data-end="898">
<h2 data-start="900" data-end="921"><strong data-start="903" data-end="921">2. Lamphrodyne</strong></h2>
<ul data-start="922" data-end="1454">
<li data-start="922" data-end="978">
<p data-start="924" data-end="978"><strong data-start="924" data-end="935">Domain:</strong> Cosmology / vacuum dynamics / negentropy</p>
</li>
<li data-start="979" data-end="1129">
<p data-start="981" data-end="1001"><strong data-start="981" data-end="999">Core Elements:</strong></p>
<ul data-start="1004" data-end="1129">
<li data-start="1004" data-end="1071">
<p data-start="1006" data-end="1071">Encodes <strong data-start="1014" data-end="1042">directional entropy flux</strong> (negentropic vacuum flows)</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1074" data-end="1129">
<p data-start="1076" data-end="1129">Modulates space-time smoothing and field recursions</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-start="1130" data-end="1314">
<p data-start="1132" data-end="1147"><strong data-start="1132" data-end="1145">Function:</strong></p>
<ul data-start="1150" data-end="1314">
<li data-start="1150" data-end="1235">
<p data-start="1152" data-end="1235">Maintains <strong data-start="1162" data-end="1183">dynamic stability</strong> of the plenum by counteracting excessive entropy.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1238" data-end="1314">
<p data-start="1240" data-end="1314">Influences scalar-vector dynamics in RSVP, producing emergent structure.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-start="1315" data-end="1454">
<p data-start="1317" data-end="1454"><strong data-start="1317" data-end="1335">NFT Signature:</strong> The <strong data-start="1340" data-end="1364">negentropic operator</strong>, the “signature brushstroke” that differentiates one universe configuration from another.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="1456" data-end="1459">
<h2 data-start="1461" data-end="1522"><strong data-start="1464" data-end="1522">3. Geometric Bayesianism with Sparse Heuristics (GBSH)</strong></h2>
<ul data-start="1523" data-end="2197">
<li data-start="1523" data-end="1591">
<p data-start="1525" data-end="1591"><strong data-start="1525" data-end="1536">Domain:</strong> Cognitive inference / navigation in curved manifolds</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1592" data-end="1833">
<p data-start="1594" data-end="1614"><strong data-start="1594" data-end="1612">Core Elements:</strong></p>
<ul data-start="1617" data-end="1833">
<li data-start="1617" data-end="1678">
<p data-start="1619" data-end="1678">Sparse heuristics → proxy jumps for efficient computation</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1681" data-end="1753">
<p data-start="1683" data-end="1753">Bayesian updates → probabilistic guidance over information manifolds</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1756" data-end="1833">
<p data-start="1758" data-end="1833">Geometric manifolds → encode dependency, constraint, and causal structure</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-start="1834" data-end="2065">
<p data-start="1836" data-end="1851"><strong data-start="1836" data-end="1849">Function:</strong></p>
<ul data-start="1854" data-end="2065">
<li data-start="1854" data-end="1965">
<p data-start="1856" data-end="1965">Governs <strong data-start="1864" data-end="1910">navigation of cognitive or decision spaces</strong> efficiently, respecting energy/metabolic constraints</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1968" data-end="2065">
<p data-start="1970" data-end="2065">Integrates with RSVP entropy fields to guide inference, acting as a <strong data-start="2038" data-end="2063">cognitive map overlay</strong></p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-start="2066" data-end="2197">
<p data-start="2068" data-end="2197"><strong data-start="2068" data-end="2086">NFT Signature:</strong> The <strong data-start="2091" data-end="2116">cognitive fingerprint</strong>; no two agents’ heuristic trajectories are identical even in the same substrate.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="2199" data-end="2202">
<h2 data-start="2204" data-end="2224"><strong data-start="2207" data-end="2224">4. Youtronium</strong></h2>
<ul data-start="2225" data-end="2741">
<li data-start="2225" data-end="2287">
<p data-start="2227" data-end="2287"><strong data-start="2227" data-end="2238">Domain:</strong> Fictional corporation / speculative meta-frame</p>
