data-start="0" data-end="244">Exactly—that’s a very natural generalization. Anything that leaves a <strong data-start="69" data-end="94">distinctive footprint</strong> in your workflow or project structure can be thought of as a “non-fungible token” in a conceptual sense, even if it’s not a literal blockchain NFT.</p>
<p data-start="246" data-end="260">For example:</p>
<ol data-start="262" data-end="1195">
<li data-start="262" data-end="525">
<p data-start="265" data-end="298"><strong data-start="265" data-end="296">File &amp; directory structure:</strong></p>
<ul data-start="302" data-end="525">
<li data-start="302" data-end="525">
<p data-start="304" data-end="525">The way you organize drafts, archives, and outputs creates a unique signature. Two people might write similar content, but your exact folder hierarchy, naming conventions, and timestamps encode your workflow’s identity.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-start="527" data-end="761">
<p data-start="530" data-end="566"><strong data-start="530" data-end="564">Scripts and automation habits:</strong></p>
<ul data-start="570" data-end="761">
<li data-start="570" data-end="761">
<p data-start="572" data-end="761">Small shell scripts, text extractors, or automated formatting routines are like “procedural fingerprints.” Even if the output text is generic, the method you used to produce it is unique.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-start="763" data-end="975">
<p data-start="766" data-end="805"><strong data-start="766" data-end="803">Stylistic and operational quirks:</strong></p>
<ul data-start="809" data-end="975">
<li data-start="809" data-end="975">
<p data-start="811" data-end="975">How you leave comments in code or notes in drafts, which tools you use for editing, the order in which you run tasks—these behavioral patterns are uniquely yours.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-start="977" data-end="1195">
<p data-start="980" data-end="1013"><strong data-start="980" data-end="1011">Project evolution patterns:</strong></p>
<ul data-start="1017" data-end="1195">
<li data-start="1017" data-end="1195">
<p data-start="1019" data-end="1195">The sequence in which drafts develop, how revisions are applied, when and where you store intermediates—all of this defines a <strong data-start="1145" data-end="1170">dynamic, temporal NFT</strong> of your working style.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ol>
<p data-start="1197" data-end="1469">So in a broad sense, anything that encodes <strong data-start="1240" data-end="1308">your habitual choices, structural patterns, or procedural traces</strong> is conceptually non-fungible—it cannot be exactly reproduced by anyone else, even if they follow your instructions. It’s an “identity token” of your workflow.</p>
<p data-start="1471" data-end="1679" data-is-last-node="" data-is-only-node="">If you want, I can suggest a <strong data-start="1500" data-end="1571">compact way to formalize this as a generalized “workflow NFT” model</strong> that applies to text, code, and project habits. It wouldn’t require blockchain at all—just the abstraction.</p></div></div></div></div><div class="flex min-h-[46px] justify-start"><div class="touch:-me-2 touch:-ms-3.5 -ms-2.5 -me-1 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-y-4 p-1 select-none touch:w-[calc(100%+--spacing(3.5))] -mt-1 w-[calc(100%+--spacing(2.5))] duration-[1.5s] focus-within:transition-none hover:transition-none pointer-events-none [mask-image:linear-gradient(to_right,black_33%,transparent_66%)] [mask-size:300%_100%] [mask-position:100%_0%] motion-safe:transition-[mask-position] group-hover/turn-messages:pointer-events-auto group-hover/turn-messages:[mask-position:0_0] group-focus-within/turn-messages:pointer-events-auto group-focus-within/turn-messages:[mask-position:0_0] has-data-[state=open]:pointer-events-auto has-data-[state=open]:[mask-position:0_0]" style="mask-position: 0% 0%;"><button class="text-token-text-secondary hover:bg-token-bg-secondary rounded-lg" aria-label="Copy" aria-pressed="false" data-testid="copy-turn-action-button" data-state="closed"><span class="flex items-center justify-center touch:w-10 h-8 w-8"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="icon"><path d="M12.668 10.667C12.668 9.95614 12.668 9.46258 12.6367 9.0791C12.6137 8.79732 12.5758 8.60761 12.5244 8.46387L12.4688 8.33399C12.3148 8.03193 12.0803 7.77885 11.793 7.60254L11.666 7.53125C11.508 7.45087 11.2963 7.39395 10.9209 7.36328C10.5374 7.33197 10.0439 7.33203 9.33301 7.33203H6.5C5.78896 7.33203 5.29563 7.33195 4.91211 7.36328C4.63016 7.38632 4.44065 7.42413 4.29688 7.47559L4.16699 7.53125C3.86488 7.68518 3.61186 7.9196 3.43555 8.20703L3.36524 8.33399C3.28478 8.49198 3.22795 8.70352 3.1972