4.66808 12.7451L4.54113 13.4619L4.14269 15.8555L4.14171 15.8574H4.14464L6.5382 15.458L7.25499 15.332C7.424 15.2977 7.5394 15.2669 7.64953 15.2266L7.80285 15.165C7.95455 15.0986 8.09947 15.0174 8.23644 14.9238L8.3839 14.8135C8.53668 14.6876 8.72225 14.5035 9.0714 14.1543L14.0587 9.16602L10.8331 5.94044L5.84581 10.9287ZM15.3634 4.63673C14.5281 3.80141 13.2057 3.74938 12.3097 4.48048L12.1368 4.63673L11.7735 5.00001L15.0001 8.22559L15.3634 7.86329L15.5196 7.68946C16.2015 6.85326 16.2015 5.64676 15.5196 4.81056L15.3634 4.63673Z"></path></svg></span></button></div></div></div></div></article><article class="text-token-text-primary w-full focus:outline-none scroll-mt-[calc(var(--header-height)+min(200px,max(70px,20svh)))]" tabindex="-1" dir="auto" data-turn-id="ab0f26cf-d890-4f79-8ac5-f2140ebe209c" data-testid="conversation-turn-52" data-scroll-anchor="false" data-turn="assistant"><h6 class="sr-only">ChatGPT said:</h6><div class="text-base my-auto mx-auto [--thread-content-margin:--spacing(4)] thread-sm:[--thread-content-margin:--spacing(6)] thread-lg:[--thread-content-margin:--spacing(16)] px-(--thread-content-margin)"><div class="[--thread-content-max-width:40rem] thread-sm:[--thread-content-max-width:40rem] thread-lg:[--thread-content-max-width:48rem] mx-auto max-w-(--thread-content-max-width) flex-1 group/turn-messages focus-visible:outline-hidden relative flex w-full min-w-0 flex-col agent-turn" tabindex="-1"><div class="flex max-w-full flex-col grow"><div data-message-author-role="assistant" data-message-id="ab0f26cf-d890-4f79-8ac5-f2140ebe209c" dir="auto" class="min-h-8 text-message relative flex w-full flex-col items-end gap-2 text-start break-words whitespace-normal [.text-message+&amp;]:mt-5" data-message-model-slug="gpt-5-mini"><div class="flex w-full flex-col gap-1 empty:hidden first:pt-[3px]"><div class="markdown prose dark:prose-invert w-full break-words dark markdown-new-styling"><p data-start="0" data-end="148">Ah, I see — you’re talking about a <strong data-start="35" data-end="83">conceptual steganographic/fingerprint system</strong> rather than a literal cryptographic pipeline. In this framing:</p>
<ol data-start="150" data-end="792">
<li data-start="150" data-end="263">
<p data-start="153" data-end="263"><strong data-start="153" data-end="217">The object itself (artwork, text, code, musical composition)</strong> is the “data” whose hash you could compute.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="264" data-end="591">
<p data-start="267" data-end="423"><strong data-start="267" data-end="285">The public key</strong> isn’t just a cryptographic key but a stand-in for the <strong data-start="340" data-end="381">knowledge, tools, or parsing pipeline</strong> needed to interpret the work correctly.</p>
<ul data-start="427" data-end="591">
<li data-start="427" data-end="521">
<p data-start="429" data-end="521">For example, knowing how to parse your unique directory structure, scripts, or neologisms.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="525" data-end="591">
<p data-start="527" data-end="591">Or knowing RSVP field semantics, or your notation conventions.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-start="592" data-end="792">
<p data-start="595" data-end="649"><strong data-start="595" data-end="632">Viewing or understanding the work</strong> requires both:</p>
<ul data-start="653" data-end="792">
<li data-start="653" data-end="698">
<p data-start="655" data-end="698">Access to the object (hashable data), and</p>
</li>
<li data-start="702" data-end="792">
<p data-start="704" data-end="792">Access to the key (parsing pipeline, background knowledge, or interpretive procedure).</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ol>
<p data-start="794" data-end="808">Effectively:</p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><mtext>Accessible&nbsp;Meaning</mtext><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>hash(object)</mtext><mo separator="true">,</mo><mtext>public&nbsp;key/pipeline</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Accessible Meaning} = f(\text{hash(object)}, \text{public key/pipeline})</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8889em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="mord text"><span class="mord">Accessible&nbsp;Meaning</span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.10764em;">f</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord text"><span class="mord">hash(object)</span></span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord text"><span class="mord">public&nbsp;key/pipeline</span></span><span class="mclose">)</span></span></span></span></span>
<ul data-start="896" data-end="1117">
<li data-start="896" data-end="942">
<p data-start="898" data-end="942">The hash ensures integrity and uniqueness.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="943" data-end="1012">
<p data-start="945" data-end="1012">The key defines <strong data-start="961" data-end="1009">who can read it or how it can be interpreted</strong>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1013" data-end="1117">
<p data-start="1015" data-end="1117">Any deviation in either (object modified or wrong parsing knowledge) prevents proper interpretation.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="1119" data-end="1300">This is exactly like a <strong data-start="1142" data-end="1177">non-fungible token in principle</strong> but conceptualized epistemically rather than economically: it ties a unique artifact to a unique <em data-start="1275" data-end="1297">interpretive context</em>.</p>
<p data-start="1302" data-end="1473" data-is-last-node="" data-is-only-node="">If you want, I can give a <strong data-start="1328" data-end="1423">small illustrative mapping showing neologisms + workflow + parsing key → unique fingerprint</strong> in this exact framing. It would be very concrete.</p></div></div></div></div><div class="flex min-h-[46px] justify-start"><div class="touch:-me-2 touch:-ms-3.5 -ms-2.5 -me-1 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-y-4 p-1 select-none touch:w-[calc(100%+--spacing(3.5))] -mt-1 w-[calc(100%+--spacing(2.5))] duration-[1.5s] focus-within:transition-none hover:transition-none pointer-events-none [mask-image:linear-gradient(to_right,black_33%,transparent_66%)] [mask-size:300%_100%] [mask-position:100%_0%] motion-safe:transition-[mask-position] group-hover/turn-messages:pointer-events-auto group-hover/turn-messages:[mask-position:0_0] group-focus-within/turn-messages:pointer-events-auto group-focus-within/turn-messages:[mask-position:0_0] has-data-[state=open]:pointer-events-auto has-data-[state=open]:[mask-position:0_0]" style="mask-position: 0% 0%;"><button class="text-token-text-secondary hover:bg-token-bg-secondary rounded-lg" aria-label="Copy" aria-pressed="false" data-testid="copy-turn-action-button" data-state="closed"><span class="flex items-center justify-center touch:w-10 h-8 w-8"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="icon"><path d="M12.668 10.667C12.668 9.95614 12.668 9.46258 12.6367 9.0791C12.6137 8.79732 12.5758 8.60761 12.5244 8.46387L12.4688 8.33399C12.3148 8.03193 12.0803 7.77885 11.793 7.60254L11.666 7.53125C11.508 7.45087 11.2963 7.39395 10.9209 7.36328C10.5374 7.33197 10.0439 7.33203 9.33301 7.33203H6.5C5.78896 7.33203 5.29563 7.33195 4.91211 7.36328C4.63016 7.38632 4.44065 7.42413 4.29688 7.47559L4.16699 7.53125C3.86488 7.68518 3.61186 7.9196 3.43555 8.20703L3.36524 8.33399C3.28478 8.49198 3.22795 8.70352 3.19727 9.0791C3.16595 9.46259 3.16504 9.95