<ul data-start="4162" data-end="4480">
<li data-start="4162" data-end="4194">
<p data-start="4164" data-end="4194">Objects = artifact + context</p>
</li>
<li data-start="4195" data-end="4246">
<p data-start="4197" data-end="4246">Morphisms = semantic-preserving transformations</p>
</li>
<li data-start="4247" data-end="4336">
<p data-start="4249" data-end="4336">Functor <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.13889em;">F</span></span></span></span> = identifies observers/pipelines capable of interpreting the artifact</p>
</li>
<li data-start="4337" data-end="4406">
<p data-start="4339" data-end="4406">Monoidal structure = artifact composition under combined contexts</p>
</li>
<li data-start="4407" data-end="4480">
<p data-start="4409" data-end="4480">Non-fungibility = non-isomorphism of objects across distinct contexts</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="4482" data-end="4485">
<p data-start="4487" data-end="4674">This sets up a <strong data-start="4502" data-end="4539">rigorous category-theoretic model</strong> of artifacts, workflows, neologisms, and cryptographic fingerprints entirely aligned with RSVP and your semantic module perspective.</p>
<p data-start="4676" data-end="4945">If you like, I can <strong data-start="4695" data-end="4752">combine this with your sheaf-theoretic interpretation</strong> into a <strong data-start="4760" data-end="4800">single, higher-categorical formalism</strong> where sections, fibers, and functors coexist naturally. This would fully capture NFT-like uniqueness under epistemic and workflow constraints.</p>
