ata-start="0" data-end="106">Here’s a <strong data-start="9" data-end="39">category-theoretic mapping</strong> of your idea using the plain-language analogy we just discussed:</p>
<hr data-start="108" data-end="111">
<h3 data-start="113" data-end="127">1. Objects</h3>
<ul data-start="129" data-end="442">
<li data-start="129" data-end="246">
<p data-start="131" data-end="246">Each <strong data-start="136" data-end="148">artifact</strong> (text, painting, workflow, draft, or idea) is an <strong data-start="198" data-end="208">object</strong> <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo separator="true">,</mo><mi>B</mi><mo separator="true">,</mo><mi>C</mi><mo separator="true">,</mo><mo>…</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A, B, C, \dots</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8778em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">A</span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05017em;">B</span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.07153em;">C</span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="minner">…</span></span></span></span> in the category.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="247" data-end="367">
<p data-start="249" data-end="367">Its <strong data-start="253" data-end="271">context folder</strong> (scripts, notes, draft hierarchy, unique workflow) can also be considered part of the object.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="368" data-end="442">
<p data-start="370" data-end="442">Formally, an object is a <strong data-start="395" data-end="403">pair</strong> <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>artifact</mtext><mo separator="true">,</mo><mtext>context</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\text{artifact}, \text{context})</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord text"><span class="mord">artifact</span></span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord text"><span class="mord">context</span></span><span class="mclose">)</span></span></span></span>.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="444" data-end="447">
<h3 data-start="449" data-end="465">2. Morphisms</h3>
<ul data-start="467" data-end="895">
<li data-start="467" data-end="617">
<p data-start="469" data-end="617">A <strong data-start="471" data-end="483">morphism</strong> <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>:</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>→</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f: A \to B</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8889em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.10764em;">f</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">:</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">A</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">→</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05017em;">B</span></span></span></span> represents a <strong data-start="512" data-end="542">viewing or parsing process</strong>—the key or pipeline required to interpret <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">A</span></span></span></span> in the context of <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05017em;">B</span></span></span></span>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="618" data-end="754">
<p data-start="620" data-end="754">If you change your workflow or scripts, the morphism changes: the same artifact may be interpreted differently with a different key.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="755" data-end="895">
<p data-start="757" data-end="895">Morphisms respect composition: if <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>:</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>→</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f: A \to B</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8889em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.10764em;">f</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">:</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">A</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">→</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05017em;">B</span></span></span></span> and <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>:</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>→</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g: B \to C</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.625em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.03588em;">g</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">:</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05017em;">B</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">→</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.07153em;">C</span></span></span></span>, then <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>∘</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>:</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>→</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g \circ f: A \to C</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6389em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.03588em;">g</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">∘</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8889em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.10764em;">f</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">:</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">A</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">→</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.07153em;">C</span></span></span></span> is the composite interpretation pipeline.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="897" data-end="900">
<h3 data-start="902" data-end="927">3. Identity Morphisms</h3>
<ul data-start="929" data-end="1137">
<li data-start="929" data-end="1078">
<p data-start="931" data-end="1078">Each object has an <strong data-start="950" data-end="971">identity morphism</strong> <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><msub><mtext>id</mtext><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>:</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>→</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{id}_A: A \to A</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8444em; vertical-align: -0.15em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord text"><span class="mord">id</span></span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3283em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">A</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">:</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">A</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">→</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">A</span></span></span></span>, representing “interpreting the artifact with its native context and workflow.”</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1079" data-end="1137">
<p data-start="1081" data-end="1137">This ensures full understanding without any translation.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="1139" data-end="1142">
<h3 data-start="1144" data-end="1166">4. Non-Fungibility</h3>
<ul data-start="1168" data-end="1429">
<li data-start="1168" data-end="1278">
<p data-start="1170" data-end="1278">No two objects <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo separator="true">,</mo><msub><mtext>context</mtext><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(A, \text{context}_1)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal">A</span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord text"><span class="mord">context</span></span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3011em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight">1</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mclose">)</span></span></span></span> and <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo separator="true">,</mo><msub><mtext>context</mtext><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(A, \text{context}_2)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal">A</span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord text"><span class="mord">context</span></span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3011em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight">2</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mclose">)</span></span></span></span> are equal if their contexts differ.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1279" data-end="1429">
<p data-start="1281" data-end="1429">Even if the content of the artifact is identical, the morphisms (keys/pipelines) differ, making them <strong data-start="1382" data-end="1398">non-fungible</strong> in category-theoretic terms.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="1431" data-end="1434">
<h3 data-start="1436" data-end="1487">5. Combining Artifacts (Functorial Perspective)</h3>
<ul data-start="1489" data-end="1914">
<li data-start="1489" data-end="1552">
<p data-start="1491" data-end="1552">Suppose you merge two artifacts <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">A</span></span></span></span> and <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05017em;">B</span></span></span></span> into <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.07153em;">C</span></span></span></span>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1553" data-end="1748">
<p data-start="1555" data-end="1748">You can model this as a <strong data-start="1579" data-end="1590">functor</strong> <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>:</mo><mi mathvariant="script">C</mi><mo>×</mo><mi mathvariant="script">C</mi><mo>→</mo><mi mathvariant="script">C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F: \mathcal{C} \times \mathcal{C} \to \mathcal{C}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.13889em;">F</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">:</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.7667em; vertical-align: -0.0833em;"></span><span class="mord mathcal" style="margin-right: 0.05834em;">C</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">×</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathcal" style="margin-right: 0.05834em;">C</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">→</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathcal" style="margin-right: 0.05834em;">C</span></span></span></span>, mapping pairs of objects (and their morphisms) to a new object that preserves context relationships.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1749" data-end="1914">
<p data-start="1751" data-end="1914">The resulting object <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.07153em;">C</span></span></span></span> is fully interpretable only through the <strong data-start="1818" data-end="1840">composed morphisms</strong> from <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">A</span></span></span></span> and <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05017em;">B</span></span></span></span>, maintaining non-fungibility and context dependence.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="1916" data-end="1919">
<h3 data-start="1921" data-end="1949">6. Sparse Interpretation</h3>
<ul data-start="1951" data-end="2223">
<li data-start="1951" data-end="2033">
<p data-start="1953" data-end="2033">Some morphisms may “ignore” part of the context, giving partial understanding.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2034" data-end="2076">
<p data-start="2036" data-end="2076">Others fully respect the full context.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2077" data-end="2223">
<p data-start="2079" data-end="2223">This aligns with your <strong data-start="2101" data-end="2129">sparse heuristics / GBSH</strong> idea: inference can be done efficiently along selected pathways without needing every detail.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="2225" data-end="2228">
<h3 data-start="2230" data-end="2243">✅ Summary</h3>
<div class="_tableContainer_1rjym_1"><div tabindex="-1" class="_tableWrapper_1rjym_13 group flex w-fit flex-col-reverse"><table data-start="2245" data-end="3307" class="w-fit min-w-(--thread-content-width)"><thead data-start="2245" data-end="2364"><tr data-start="2245" data-end="2364"><th data-start="2245" data-end="2270" data-col-size="sm">Concept</th><th data-start="2270" data-end="2318" data-col-size="md">Category-Theoretic Representation</th><th data-start="2318" data-end="2364" data-col-size="md">Analogy</th></tr></thead><tbody data-start="2482" data-end="3307"><tr data-start="2482" data-end="2600"><td data-start="2482" data-end="2507" data-col-size="sm">Artifact</td><td data-start="2507" data-end="2554" data-col-size="md">Object <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">A</span></span></span></span></td><td data-start="2554" data-end="2600" data-col-size="md">File / draft / painting</td></tr><tr data-start="2601" data-end="2716"><td data-start="2601" data-end="2626" data-col-size="sm">Context &amp; Workflow</td><td data-start="2626" data-end="2672" data-col-size="md">Part of object <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo separator="true">,</mo><mtext>context</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(A, \text{context})</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal">A</span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspa