n class="mord text mtight"><span class="mord mtight">global</span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.2861em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6444em;"></span><span class="mord">0</span></span></span></span></span>
<p data-start="484" data-end="715">expresses a <strong data-start="496" data-end="533">conservation of entropic “charge”</strong>: any negentropic action in a local semantic module is counterbalanced by entropy elsewhere in the system. This reframes paradoxes as <strong data-start="667" data-end="693">structural necessities</strong> rather than failures.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="717" data-end="1068">
<p data-start="720" data-end="756"><strong data-start="720" data-end="754">Lamphron–Lamphrodyne Polarity:</strong></p>
<ul data-start="760" data-end="1068">
<li data-start="760" data-end="809">
<p data-start="762" data-end="809"><strong data-start="762" data-end="776">Lamphrons:</strong> Local attractors of coherence.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="813" data-end="1068">
<p data-start="815" data-end="1068"><strong data-start="815" data-end="832">Lamphrodynes:</strong> Global dispersers of entropy.<br data-start="862" data-end="865">
Contradictions arise when <strong data-start="894" data-end="934">lamphron clustering succeeds locally</strong>, but <strong data-start="940" data-end="989">lamphrodyne flows disperse the gains globally</strong>, creating the characteristic push–pull of critique vs. systemic reinforcement.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-start="1070" data-end="1471">
<p data-start="1073" data-end="1167"><strong data-start="1073" data-end="1111">Category-Theoretic Interpretation:</strong><br data-start="1111" data-end="1114">
Each contradiction is a <strong data-start="1141" data-end="1164">commutative diagram</strong>:</p>
