<p data-start="3245" data-end="3366">illustrates how a single action simultaneously stabilizes local coherence while being absorbed into systemic dispersal.</p>
<h4 data-start="3368" data-end="3427"><strong data-start="3373" data-end="3427">5. Lamphron–Lamphrodyne Polarity – Bridging Scales</strong></h4>
<p data-start="3429" data-end="3555">The interplay of lamphrons (local attractors) and lamphrodynes (global dispersers) <strong data-start="3512" data-end="3552">formalizes the paradoxes of critique</strong>:</p>
<ul data-start="3557" data-end="3753">
<li data-start="3557" data-end="3619">
<p data-start="3559" data-end="3619">Lamphrons cluster negentropy and preserve local coherence.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="3620" data-end="3753">
<p data-start="3622" data-end="3753">Lamphrodynes diffuse entropy across global networks, ensuring that no single critique or innovation can escape systemic coupling.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="3755" data-end="3915">Together, they reveal that paradoxes are <strong data-start="3796" data-end="3824">thermodynamic invariants</strong> of the socio-technical system: coherent action is inseparable from its global dispersal.</p>
<hr data-start="3917" data-end="3920">
<p data-start="3922" data-end="4145">If you want, the next section can <strong data-start="3956" data-end="4064">extend this mapping to neologisms, unique workflows, cryptographic signatures, and intellectual products</strong>, showing how these act as semantic “fingerprints” in the RSVP field framework.</p>
